  body: "# Assessing a capital disregard for JSA(IB) and IS\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured
    chapter requires evidence for a capital disregard, places the disregard question before valuation
    and says all applicable disregards for an item must be considered because they can affect income treatment.\n\
    \n## Scope and exceptions\n\nEach disregard has its own conditions and period; no blanket duration
    or current capital threshold is inferred. DMG 29351 carries a memo 11/20 call-out. The procedure resembles
    other chapters but does not establish equivalence with Pension Credit, and its source wording is not
    a specialist-approved rule.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 29351, PDF page 43](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f3a496c86b751317022c/dmg-Ch-29.pdf#page=43)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 29: Capital.\n- [DMG 29352, PDF page 43](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f3a496c86b751317022c/dmg-Ch-29.pdf#page=43)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 29: Capital.\n- [DMG 29353, PDF page 43](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f3a496c86b751317022c/dmg-Ch-29.pdf#page=43)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 29: Capital.\n- [DMG 29354, PDF page 43](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f3a496c86b751317022c/dmg-Ch-29.pdf#page=43)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 29: Capital.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation of selected
    passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required. Source acquisition,
    source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\nThis is an
    independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice, an entitlement
    decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes and characters.
    No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is claimed by this
    record.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch29`: PDF SHA-256 `a1b086fdad8d32d6273b35fb8895516b6957faacd05fd3b06e091032598a47b9`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `b490507e3aaf6110ea0593fee2ee4d772fd5a1f9a75f4f91008734caec51cfd9`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-burden-of-proof
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The capital-disregard passage expressly identifies the claimant’s evidential burden
      for this specific question; this must not become a rule that the claimant bears every burden.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch29/0043
      quote: "29352 The claimant has to show that the capital can be disregarded. If there is no evidence
        to show\ncapital can be disregarded, it is included when working out the amount of capital a claimant
        has."
      locator: DMG 29352
  - target: term/jsais-income-capital-distinction
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explains that certain capital disregards affect whether income from that
      capital is treated as income rather than capital.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch29/0043
      quote: "29354 The DM decides all of the disregards which apply to each item of capital. This is
        because income\nfrom capital is taken into account as income and not capital if certain disregards
        apply. DMs should note\nthat this also applies if the capital is worth nothing."
      locator: DMG 29354
